---
// Three states, cycling system -> light -> dark -> system. "System" is a real
// state rather than an implicit default, so a visitor can always get back to
// following their OS without clearing site data.
//
// Rendered TWICE per page since issue #101: once in SiteHeader's desktop right
// cluster and once in MobileNav's overlay, because putting that cluster behind
// `lg` took the control away from every phone. The behaviour moved to
// src/lib/theme-toggle.ts when the second one arrived -- a click has to repaint
// every instance, not the one it landed on, and that is only assertable
// against a DOM. Astro hoists this script once however many times the
// component is used, so two buttons still mean one script.
---

<button
  type="button"
  data-theme-toggle
  aria-label="Theme: follow system"
  class="border border-rule px-2.5 py-2 font-mono text-micro text-ink"
>
  <span data-theme-label>SYSTEM</span>
</button>

<script>
  import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme-toggle';

  initThemeToggle();
</script>
